WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
In 2018, Scotland did something unusual.

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.570
It pushed a price up,

3
00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:10.100
on purpose. It set a minimum
price for every unit of alcohol:

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:15.200
50 pence. In 2024, that rose to 65 pence.

5
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.160
So a 70 centilitre bottle of 40 per cent

6
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.560
spirit cannot legally sell
for less than 18 pounds 20.

7
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.120
Why would a government ever
make something cost more?

8
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.900
In this mission, you'll draw a
minimum price above equilibrium,

9
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.470
and see how buyers and sellers respond.

10
00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:36.030
Then you'll raise a guaranteed
price for farmers yourself,

11
00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.210
and track what it costs the government.

12
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:41.320
Your mission: find out why
a government would ever

13
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.920
make something cost more.
